{% extends "layouts/app.njk" %}
{% from "govuk/components/summary-list/macro.njk" import govukSummaryList %}
{% from "govuk/components/character-count/macro.njk" import govukCharacterCount %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}
{% from "govuk/components/error-summary/macro.njk" import govukErrorSummary %}

{#
  Step one of the send-an-email journey: the free-text slots, pre-populated.

  THE CONTROLS ARE api's SLOT METADATA, not a form written here. One `EmailSlotResponse` row per control — its
  name, its cap and whether it is required — so a template api adds later renders its own fields with no change
  in this file. That is why there is a loop rather than two named controls.

  THE CONTROL NAMES ARE `snake_case` AND MUST STAY THAT WAY. They are GOV.UK Notify placeholder names, which
  makes each one the personalisation key, the request-body key and the field api's own 400 addresses itself to at
  once. Renaming one to this repo's camelCase convention breaks the personalisation silently: Notify substitutes
  nothing and the applicant reads the template with an empty quotation in it.

  Character counts rather than `maxlength`, the call witness-form.njk and referral-form.njk both record: the cap
  is api's and is stated in the message, and a browser that silently stops accepting characters gives no reason
  for having done so. A caseworker over the cap is asked to shorten the wording, never truncated — a shortened
  quotation of a judge is worse than being asked to shorten one.

  The form posts to the check page, which is mandatory because sending is irreversible. Decision 2 of
  docs/plans/notify-2-caseworker-email-tab.md.
#}
{% block content %}
<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">

    {% if errorList.length %}
      {{ govukErrorSummary({ titleText: errorSummaryTitle, errorList: errorList }) }}
    {% endif %}

    <span class="govuk-caption-l">{{ case.displayReference }}</span>
    <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl govuk-!-margin-bottom-4">{{ heading }}</h1>

    {{ govukSummaryList({ rows: [ { key: { text: templateLabel }, value: { text: compose.name } } ] }) }}

    <p class="govuk-body">{{ intro }}</p>
    <p class="govuk-hint">{{ prePopulatedHint }}</p>

    <form method="post" action="/deed-polls/{{ case.id }}/emails/{{ compose.template }}/preview" novalidate>
      {#
        The journey's token, carried unchanged from the moment the form opened. Admin-local: it goes to the check
        page and back here on a correction, and never to api — see journeyToken in compose.ts.
      #}
      <input type="hidden" name="{{ journeyField }}" value="{{ token }}">

      {% for f in compose.fields %}
        {{ govukCharacterCount({
          id: f.name,
          name: f.name,
          rows: 8,
          maxlength: f.maxLength,
          value: f.value,
          label: { text: f.label if f.required else f.label + " " + optional, classes: "govuk-label--m" },
          errorMessage: { text: errors[f.name] } if errors[f.name]
        }) }}
      {% endfor %}

      <div class="govuk-button-group">
        {{ govukButton({ text: submit }) }}
        <a class="govuk-link" href="/deed-polls/{{ case.id }}#emails">{{ cancel }}</a>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
